  "format": "opensculptboy.joint-ranges/1",
  "about": "The range of each bone's turn (degrees) in its own joint frame, for the posing solves (opensculptboy.posing.point_solve) and the web page's pose editor. A bone's twist axis runs from its head to the head of `next`; its bend axis turns the bone's end towards `toward`; a finger's bend axis is its `hinge` instead (the right hand's, in the reference pose's axes: the axis of its turn in the library fist `mh_fight`, as `opensculptboy.statues.hands.key_hand` keys a finger; the left hand's is its mirror image), and its twist axis runs along the bone square to it; the side axis is the third. Bend, side and twist mean the same on both sides of the figure (the left side's side and twist are mirrored). `dofs` lists the axes a solve may turn: b (bend), s (side), t (twist); a bone in a twist group turns about the group's axis by its share as well. The ranges follow the usual clinical ranges of motion, measured from Anny's reference pose and widened a little for carved and stylised figures; a solve can switch them off.",
